
Act as a Principal AI Architect.

Objective:
Establish the Knowledge Base as the governed enterprise knowledge source for all AI consumers, including:
- Knowledge Assistant
- Future AI Agents
- Ticketing systems (ServiceNow/Jira/Zendesk/Freshservice)
- MCP tools
- LangSmith evaluation pipelines
- Future enterprise copilots

Design and implement an enterprise knowledge platform instead of a chatbot-only solution.

====================================
Requirements
====================================

1. Single Source of Truth
- All AI systems must retrieve knowledge only from the KB.
- No duplicate knowledge stores.
- Every answer must originate from approved KB content.

2. Governed Knowledge
Each article must support:
- Draft
- Review
- Approved
- Archived
- Version history
- Approval workflow
- Owner
- Reviewer
- Last modified
- Effective date
- Expiration date

Only Approved articles may be retrieved by AI.

3. Shared Retrieval Service
Create one centralized Retrieval Service that is used by:
- KB Assistant
- MCP Server
- GitHub Integration
- Future Ticketing integrations
- LangSmith evaluation
- Future APIs

Avoid duplicate retrieval logic.

4. MCP Integration
Expose enterprise tools such as:
- SearchKnowledge
- SearchDocuments
- SearchHierarchy
- GetArticle
- GetMetadata
- SearchGitHub
- SearchConfluence (future)
- SearchSharePoint (future)
- SearchTickets (future)

All AI consumers must use these tools.

5. Ticketing Integration
Design APIs so ticket systems can:
- Search KB before ticket creation
- Recommend existing articles
- Suggest troubleshooting steps
- Generate draft responses using approved KB content
- Link KB articles to tickets
- Record article usage analytics

6. LangSmith Readiness
Expose retrieval pipeline for LangSmith.
Capture:
- User question
- Retrieved chunks
- Source articles
- Metadata
- Confidence score
- Citations
- Latency
- LLM response
- User feedback

7. Grounded AI
The assistant must:
- Answer only from retrieved evidence.
- Never hallucinate.
- Say "I could not find information in the Knowledge Base" if evidence is insufficient.
- Always include citations.

8. Knowledge APIs
Provide reusable APIs:

GET /api/knowledge/search
GET /api/knowledge/article/:id
GET /api/knowledge/hierarchy
GET /api/knowledge/documents
GET /api/knowledge/metadata

These APIs must be reusable by every application.

9. Analytics
Create dashboards showing:
- Most searched topics
- Failed searches
- Article usage
- AI answer success rate
- Ticket deflection
- Top referenced articles
- Stale content
- Articles needing review

10. Security
Respect existing RBAC.
Users may retrieve only content they are authorized to access.
Draft and restricted content must never be exposed.

11. Architecture
Refactor into:

Knowledge Repository
↓
Embedding Index
↓
Retrieval Service
↓
MCP Layer
↓
AI Consumers
   • Knowledge Assistant
   • Ticket Systems
   • LangSmith
   • Future AI Agents

12. Extensibility
Support future integrations without changing retrieval logic:
- Jira
- ServiceNow
- Zendesk
- Freshservice
- Slack
- Microsoft Teams
- SharePoint
- Confluence
- GitHub
- Azure DevOps

13. Deliverables
- Architecture diagram
- Database changes (if required)
- API contracts
- Retrieval flow
- MCP tool definitions
- Folder structure
- Implementation plan
- Unit tests
- Integration tests
- Documentation

Do not break existing functionality. Extend the current KB Admin architecture using the existing Anthropic-based Retrieval and MCP implementation.
